  "worked_solution": "From the graph of the function $f(y),$ we can deduce the following information:\n\n- The solutions to $f(y)=0$ are $y=5$ and $y=7.$ Therefore $y=5,7$ are the equilibrium solutions of the differential equation.\n\n- $f(y)>0$ when $y\\in (-\\infty ,5)\\cup (7,\\infty ).$\n\n- $f(y)<0$ when $y\\in (5,7).$\n\nTherefore, we can draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14094575/assets/6fe54fbeff8bef87f572955c9f441bcc537cea3dd8e07046f6ef121ff3b95e94.png)",
